{
  // The private dashboard — a SECOND Worker, separate from the public site.
  //
  // Assets only, no server code: `npm run dashboard` builds apps/dashboard/dist/
  // (index.html + data.json + your tokens) and Workers serves that folder. The
  // gate is a Cloudflare Access policy attached to this Worker, not code in it,
  // which is why there is no fetch handler here to get wrong.
  //
  // Deploy with:  npm run deploy:dashboard
  // Then attach Access once, in the dashboard: Workers & Pages → this Worker →
  // Access → Protect this Worker. See docs/deploy-cloudflare.md ▸ private.
  //
  // Tick boxes (source/formats/dashboard.md ▸ Tick boxes): for pages that tick a line of a to-do
  // file, this Worker runs the to-do app's code, which checks the Access token of every request,
  // serves these pages and answers /api/todos. Then add, in this file:
  //   "main": "../todos/worker.js",
  //   "workers_dev": false,
  //   "assets": { "directory": "./dist", "binding": "ASSETS", "run_worker_first": true,
  //               "not_found_handling": "404-page", "html_handling": "auto-trailing-slash" },
  //   "vars": { "TEAM_DOMAIN": "https://<team>.cloudflareaccess.com", "POLICY_AUD": "<this app's AUD>",
  //             "TODO_BRANCH": "main", "TODO_SOURCES": [ … from `node scripts/todo-sources.mjs --intranet` ] }
  // and the token once: wrangler secret put GITHUB_TOKEN --config apps/dashboard/wrangler.jsonc
  // `npm run check` refuses the combination that would leave a page open or every page refused.
  //
  // Set `name` during setup: <your-slug>-dashboard, unique in your account. It is
  // also its <name>.<subdomain>.workers.dev hostname, which Access covers too.
  "$schema": "../../node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "my-dashboard",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-08-23",
  "assets": {
    "directory": "./dist"
  }
}
